       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg once daily. At that dose the patient could have severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged peripheral vasodilation. Amlodipine's long half-life (30 to 50 hours) would make an overdose last a long time.\n\nPlease check which of these applies:\n- **Typo:** you may have meant 5 mg once daily, which is the usual starting dose, or 10 mg once daily, which is the maximum.\n- **Intentional dose:** if 50 mg is really intended, I'd need you to confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I'd also suggest a pharmacist review first.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order right away. For example: amlodipine 5 mg, oral, once daily."
